WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:01.708
- [Woman] Wait, are you serious?

00:00:01.708 --> 00:00:02.541
- Yeah, what's wrong with this?

00:00:02.541 --> 00:00:04.424
- [Woman] You look like you're
about to go to a hockey game.

00:00:04.424 --> 00:00:05.906
- What's wrong with that?

00:00:05.906 --> 00:00:07.850
- [Woman] You're not
going to a hockey game.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.292
(both laughing)

00:00:10.292 --> 00:00:11.282
- Sister knows best.

00:00:11.282 --> 00:00:12.430
- [Woman] Yes.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:15.263
(energetic music)

00:00:16.403 --> 00:00:18.581
- I'm going to be getting
a sibling for a week.

00:00:18.581 --> 00:00:20.304
Common misconceptions
of being an only child

00:00:20.304 --> 00:00:21.620
is that you don't know how to share.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.211
You want it to always be all about you.

00:00:24.211 --> 00:00:25.404
Just kinda true.

00:00:25.404 --> 00:00:26.598
I'm honestly really excited

00:00:26.598 --> 00:00:29.586
to kind of have that companionship.

00:00:29.586 --> 00:00:31.187
I've always wanted a brother.

00:00:31.187 --> 00:00:33.190
When I was younger, I went to a mall Santa

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.040
and I asked for an older
brother for Christmas.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.694
And he laughed in my face.

00:00:37.694 --> 00:00:39.912
I didn't believe in Santa for
that much longer after that.

00:00:39.912 --> 00:00:42.462
So I'm about to find out
who my sibling's gonna be.

00:00:42.462 --> 00:00:44.962
I'm so excited and also very nervous.

00:00:44.962 --> 00:00:45.954
Here we go.

00:00:45.954 --> 00:00:48.621
(lullaby music)

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:54.697
Oh, Nyla, oh I'm so happy.

00:00:54.697 --> 00:00:55.530
Oh my God.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.451
So I'm so excited.

00:00:59.451 --> 00:01:01.308
We're gonna be brother and sister.

00:01:01.308 --> 00:01:02.881
So this week my parents are coming in town

00:01:02.881 --> 00:01:06.231
for vacation so we're gonna be
cooking them a meal together

00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:07.266
but we're also going to be going on

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:08.790
a family outing together.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:09.819
- And at the end of the week,

00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:12.349
we're going to be taking
a family portrait photo.

00:01:12.349 --> 00:01:13.957
And I'm very excited for that.

00:01:13.957 --> 00:01:14.987
- Me too!

00:01:14.987 --> 00:01:16.306
I had no clue you were an only child.

00:01:16.306 --> 00:01:17.297
- Yeah, just me.

00:01:17.297 --> 00:01:18.460
- I don't know why anyone complains

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.447
about having a sibling.

00:01:19.447 --> 00:01:22.255
- Watch as we're gonna
probably be arguing by day two.

00:01:22.255 --> 00:01:25.172
- Nyla is heading down to the lobby

00:01:26.257 --> 00:01:30.027
and we're about to meet her
and go to a museum together.

00:01:30.027 --> 00:01:31.020
Are you ready?

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.095
- Yeah!

00:01:32.095 --> 00:01:34.661
- I was a little nervous at first.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.154
I know how my family operates.

00:01:36.154 --> 00:01:38.428
I don't really know how other
people's family operates.

00:01:38.428 --> 00:01:39.261
Hi guys!

00:01:40.163 --> 00:01:41.151
- Hi Nyla.

00:01:41.151 --> 00:01:42.184
- How are you, dad?

00:01:42.184 --> 00:01:45.007
But then I fell in love
with them like instantly.

00:01:45.007 --> 00:01:47.603
Didn't know you had a
daughter and now you do.

00:01:47.603 --> 00:01:49.591
You walk up to a family that's not yours,

00:01:49.591 --> 00:01:51.905
especially parents, they
either go by Mr or Mrs,

00:01:51.905 --> 00:01:53.396
something very formal.

00:01:53.396 --> 00:01:55.293
But Ben's parents were
just like, Mom and Dad.

00:01:55.293 --> 00:01:56.749
And I was like, okay cool.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:59.186
- So she just told us it
was four blocks that way.

00:01:59.186 --> 00:02:01.049
- We went to the wrong
wax museum at first.

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:02.042
- Yeah.

00:02:02.042 --> 00:02:03.249
- I think that kinda like broke the ice.

00:02:03.249 --> 00:02:04.667
- Okay kids, don't cry.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.622
We'll get you to the wax museum.

00:02:06.622 --> 00:02:07.994
- Out of family disfunction, we were able

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.602
to share that moment and
it kind of set the tone

00:02:09.602 --> 00:02:10.673
for the rest of the day.

00:02:10.673 --> 00:02:11.506
- Yeah.

00:02:11.506 --> 00:02:12.339
- We made it.

00:02:12.339 --> 00:02:13.172
- We arrived!

00:02:13.172 --> 00:02:14.005
- We're here.

00:02:14.005 --> 00:02:14.838
- All right, let's do this.

00:02:14.838 --> 00:02:15.798
- It was crazy because
at one point in time

00:02:15.798 --> 00:02:17.608
we were walking.

00:02:17.608 --> 00:02:19.308
I was kind of like a
little bit ahead of Ben

00:02:19.308 --> 00:02:21.497
and his parents and this guy.

00:02:21.497 --> 00:02:23.402
He's like, oh you should like smile more.

00:02:23.402 --> 00:02:24.926
You need a hug.

00:02:24.926 --> 00:02:27.482
- No he said, yeah, and I
was like, that's my sister.

00:02:27.482 --> 00:02:30.321
- And then your dad was like--

00:02:30.321 --> 00:02:31.437
you're about to get your ass kicked

00:02:31.437 --> 00:02:32.787
if you keep messing with her.

00:02:32.787 --> 00:02:34.109
- And I was like, okay, this is family.

00:02:34.109 --> 00:02:35.503
I'm not even worried about it.

00:02:35.503 --> 00:02:37.610
- The wax museum, we
kind of were able to like

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:40.665
break the ice and then the
family dinner the next day

00:02:40.665 --> 00:02:43.065
was also a really great time.

00:02:43.065 --> 00:02:44.138
- Where are we?

00:02:44.138 --> 00:02:45.203
- We're at Trader Joes.

00:02:45.203 --> 00:02:46.231
- We're at Trader Joes.

00:02:46.231 --> 00:02:48.125
We're going to get dinner for our parents

00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:49.828
and get groceries for the week.

00:02:49.828 --> 00:02:50.661
- Yes.

00:02:50.661 --> 00:02:51.494
Can you cook?

00:02:51.494 --> 00:02:52.327
- I can cook, yeah.

00:02:52.327 --> 00:02:53.160
- I can't.

00:02:54.489 --> 00:02:56.846
- [Ben] Mom, dad, we're home.

00:02:56.846 --> 00:02:59.321
- [Nyla] We have groceries.

00:02:59.321 --> 00:03:02.503
- It definitely felt like a family dinner.

00:03:02.503 --> 00:03:05.723
We were talking about a
lot of pretty deep things

00:03:05.723 --> 00:03:07.957
and we got into it.

00:03:07.957 --> 00:03:09.733
I took on the main course.

00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:11.162
Nyla made the salad.

00:03:11.162 --> 00:03:12.147
- The pre-made salad.

00:03:12.147 --> 00:03:12.980
- The pre-made salad.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:14.092
But I think that was
good because it was fun

00:03:14.092 --> 00:03:16.989
to make something for our parents

00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:19.048
and then also that I feel like gave

00:03:19.048 --> 00:03:20.656
an opportunity for you to really sit down

00:03:20.656 --> 00:03:21.689
and get to know them.

00:03:21.689 --> 00:03:22.675
- [Mom] Cheers, everybody.

00:03:22.675 --> 00:03:23.663
- [Everyone] Cheers!

00:03:23.663 --> 00:03:25.650
- Cheers, great for my
family to get together again.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.553
- The family dinner!

00:03:27.553 --> 00:03:30.247
- The next day we had a family photo shoot

00:03:30.247 --> 00:03:32.467
and it was corny as fuck.

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:35.805
- [Dad] It gives new meaning
to the word Facebook.

00:03:35.805 --> 00:03:37.290
- But I think at that point it was like

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.607
we were so familiar with each other.

00:03:39.607 --> 00:03:40.972
It was like so fun.

00:03:40.972 --> 00:03:43.824
And as an only child, I know
I never went to the mall

00:03:43.824 --> 00:03:47.053
and did like any sort of
portraits cause it's like,

00:03:47.053 --> 00:03:49.939
that's something you
usually do with siblings.

00:03:49.939 --> 00:03:51.141
My dad says that he's gonna send you

00:03:51.141 --> 00:03:52.627
our newsletter this year.

00:03:52.627 --> 00:03:53.662
Our family newsletter.

00:03:53.662 --> 00:03:54.655
- [Nyla] Please do.

00:03:54.655 --> 00:03:56.355
- And he wants to like
include one of those pictures.

00:03:56.355 --> 00:03:58.835
All right so we just
finished our photo shoot.

00:03:58.835 --> 00:04:00.911
- It was awesome.

00:04:00.911 --> 00:04:01.902
- Yeah?

00:04:01.902 --> 00:04:02.892
- It was a lot of fun.

00:04:02.892 --> 00:04:04.130
I don't think I've ever done that.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:07.567
- I wanna go back and do it again.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.695
- My friend Nessa, I've
known her since kindergarten.

00:04:09.695 --> 00:04:11.467
She recently moved out here and every week

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:12.785
she's been spending it with me.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.145
She spent the day and the night with us.

00:04:14.145 --> 00:04:16.746
She ends up becoming like the cousin.

00:04:16.746 --> 00:04:19.818
- We were trying to not
have to cook anything.

00:04:19.818 --> 00:04:22.735
So we got chicken and waffles and--

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.407
Look at the other side.

00:04:28.007 --> 00:04:29.424
Yeah, so I tried.

00:04:30.651 --> 00:04:32.090
We've got a whole box.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.613
- I think we both kind
of have an understanding

00:04:33.613 --> 00:04:35.060
of when it's time to be
like, oh, like let's chat.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.127
And then it's like do your thing,

00:04:37.127 --> 00:04:38.483
I'm gonna do my thing and we'll come back

00:04:38.483 --> 00:04:39.638
together eventually.

00:04:39.638 --> 00:04:40.990
- We also know common courtesy.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:42.882
Like it's different if
we were like younger

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.730
or we didn't learn manners or social cues.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.420
I think the only time we
kind of ran into anything

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.084
was like in the bathroom
because the stuff that

00:04:51.084 --> 00:04:52.854
I have to do to get ready--

00:04:52.854 --> 00:04:53.809
- Ben took the longest in the bathroom,

00:04:53.809 --> 00:04:54.920
I just would like to say.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.682
- All the stuff that I
do, I need a sink for.

00:04:56.682 --> 00:04:59.414
Like I'm not gonna shave in your kitchen.

00:04:59.414 --> 00:05:00.524
It's a process.

00:05:00.524 --> 00:05:04.325
We went out at night with your friends

00:05:04.325 --> 00:05:07.095
and it was like a situation where I was

00:05:07.095 --> 00:05:10.063
out of my element but I felt so included.

00:05:10.063 --> 00:05:12.133
It just felt like we were in it together.

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:13.286
It was fun.

00:05:13.286 --> 00:05:14.119
- Yeah.

00:05:14.119 --> 00:05:14.952
Goodnight brother.

00:05:14.952 --> 00:05:15.785
- Goodnight, sis.

00:05:15.785 --> 00:05:18.527
- I'll see you tomorrow.

00:05:18.527 --> 00:05:20.259
It's been a week since
we've been siblings.

00:05:20.259 --> 00:05:24.165
- It tried both of us like this week, wow.

00:05:24.165 --> 00:05:26.472
We're hanging out on Saturday.

00:05:26.472 --> 00:05:29.156
Nyla whips out of her garage
and we hear this thud.

00:05:29.156 --> 00:05:32.385
And then we're like, oh
my god, you hit something.

00:05:32.385 --> 00:05:33.511
And then it clicks in my head.

00:05:33.511 --> 00:05:35.165
I was like, that's my car.

00:05:35.165 --> 00:05:37.018
We turn around and sure
enough, there's my car.

00:05:37.018 --> 00:05:38.268
Parked outside.

00:05:39.331 --> 00:05:40.856
It was so funny too cause you were like,

00:05:40.856 --> 00:05:43.129
oh my god, don't tell mom and dad.

00:05:43.129 --> 00:05:46.236
They're gonna hate me,
they're gonna hate me.

00:05:46.236 --> 00:05:47.403
It was tiring.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:51.439
In times I was out of my element.

00:05:51.439 --> 00:05:55.394
But I'm so glad that I
got this time with you.

00:05:55.394 --> 00:05:58.417
I definitely feel like I consider
you family in some sense.

00:05:58.417 --> 00:06:00.235
- Yeah same.

00:06:00.235 --> 00:06:01.232
- Aw.

00:06:01.232 --> 00:06:02.265
- Same!

00:06:02.265 --> 00:06:04.168
It's like wild, we just clicked.

00:06:04.168 --> 00:06:05.166
- Yeah.

00:06:05.166 --> 00:06:07.349
You got a little peak of my family.

00:06:07.349 --> 00:06:10.406
And like, I got a peak
of your family here.

00:06:10.406 --> 00:06:12.646
The whole week there was
kind of this unspoken thing

00:06:12.646 --> 00:06:15.085
where I feel like you had
my back and I had yours.

00:06:15.085 --> 00:06:16.074
I appreciate that.

00:06:16.074 --> 00:06:17.234
- I appreciate you.

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:19.055
- Aw, I appreciate you.

00:06:19.055 --> 00:06:20.046
- I love you.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.129
- I love you.

00:06:23.473 --> 00:06:25.973
(happy music)

00:06:28.975 --> 00:06:31.123
- I'm kind of happy we
didn't share the same room.

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:32.936
I like to masturbate so--

00:06:32.936 --> 00:06:33.769
- Me too.

